* zxtn25040dz.lib - Diodes Incorporated ZXTN25040DZ, 40 V NPN medium-power transistor, SOT-89.
* VENDOR MODEL, COPIED VERBATIM FROM THE MANUFACTURER'S OWN FILE.
*
* USAGE:
*   .include models/bjt_npn/zxtn25040dz.lib
*   Q1 collector base emitter ZXTN25040DZ
*
* Role: CANDIDATE fast NPN for the complementary Class A emitter follower
* output stage (alternative to the MJE15032, whose model has CJE = 3.06 nF
* and fT 27.7 MHz, NC-024/NC-025). Complement: ZXTP25040DZ
* (models/bjt_pnp/zxtp25040dz.lib). NOT yet used by any circuit.
*
* PINOUT (datasheet DS33699 Rev. 3-2, page 1, top view pin-out figure;
* the figure carries no pin numbers): B / C / E on the three leads, the
* tab is COLLECTOR. Standard SOT-89 numbering is pin 1 = B, pin 2 = C
* (and tab), pin 3 = E - confirm against the KiCad footprint before layout.
*
* PROVENANCE - short version. Full record in
* models/bjt_npn/zxtn25040dz.provenance.json and the freeze in
* vendor/bjt_npn/diodes_inc/ZXTN25040DZ/PROVENANCE.json.
* Source: https://www.diodes.com/spice/download/2802/ZXTN25040DZ.spice.txt
* (Content-Type name="ZXTN25040DZ.spice.txt" checked, docs/limitations.md
* #21; header and .MODEL name read, #20). Frozen byte-for-byte, then
* appended below this header with NOTHING changed:
*
*   diff <(grep -v '^\*' vendor/bjt_npn/diodes_inc/ZXTN25040DZ/ZXTN25040DZ.spice.txt) \
*        <(grep -v '^\*' models/bjt_npn/zxtn25040dz.lib)      # empty
*
* The vendor file uses CRLF, this header uses LF: MIXED line endings on
* purpose, as in the other vendor-derived models. Do not normalise.
*
* CROSS-CHECK AGAINST THE DATASHEET (ngspice 47, set temp = 25, L46a):
*   fT   @ IC = 50 mA, VCE = 10 V, ftest = 100 MHz   194.7 MHz  (typ 190, no min)
*   fT   @ IC = 20 mA, VCE = 10 V (the follower)     149.4 MHz  (|hfe|=1: 149.4)
*   Cobo @ VCB = 10 V, 1 MHz                         12.18 pF   (typ 11.7, max 20)
*   hFE  @ IC = 10 mA, VCE = 2 V                     452        (min 300, typ 450)
*   hFE  @ IC = 1 A,   VCE = 2 V                     310        (min 300, typ 450)
* The model lands on the datasheet TYPICALS; the datasheet publishes no
* fT minimum. NO KF/AF in the model: NO 1/f noise, any noise figure with
* this device is a floor without flicker. CJE = 192 pF, CJC = 35 pF at
* zero bias. QUASIMOD/RCO/GAMMA are accepted by ngspice 47 with no warning.
*
